{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrhwgkqQhhHEcvjuaJmUpE","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've extracted the requirements you requested. Here's the complete verbatim text for requirements R1.1 through R1.4, including their requirement group section:\n\n---\n\n## R1: Output formats and layout (default, -1, -l, -C, -x)\n\n**R1.1:**\nWhen stdout is a TTY and no format flag is given, must produce multi-column output sorted vertically (down columns, then across). Terminal width is obtained by calling pkg/sys.TerminalWidth() (int, error) — returns the current terminal column count via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl on stdout; returns an error when stdout is not a terminal. Entries are laid out by calling pkg/format.Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string — distributes entries into the maximum number of columns fitting within termWidth, with column widths computed as per-column maxima of entry lengths.\n\n**R1.2:**\nWhen stdout is not a TTY (pipe, file redirect) and no format flag is given, must produce single-column output with one entry per line. This matches GNU ls behavior (ls.c detects stdout is not a TTY and sets format to single-column).\n\n**R1.3:**\nMust sort entries in the C locale order (LC_COLLATE=C). Differential tests must set LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent sort divergence.\n\n**R1.4:**\nMust not list entries whose names start with \".\" unless -a or -A is given. This is the default filter behavior matching GNU ls.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Goals Section\n\nThe file also contains a comprehensive non_goals section (lines 195-205):\n\n- --hyperlink (terminal hyperlinks) is out of scope for this project.\n- --dired (Emacs dired mode) is out of scope.\n- -Z (SELinux security context) is out of scope; this project does not target SELinux.\n- --quoting-style (filename quoting) is out of scope for this release.\n- --block-size=SIZE with arbitrary unit suffixes is out of scope.\n- LS_COLORS environment variable parsing is out of scope; we use GNU default colors only (srd003-format non-goals).\n- ACL (access control list) display in long format (the \"+\" indicator) is out of scope.\n- --group-directories-first is out of scope for this release.\n- -w / --width (explicit width override) is out of scope; terminal width is queried via pkg/sys.\n- --sort=WORD (long-form sort option) is out of scope; only short flags (-t, -S, -r, -U, -v) are supported."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e03b2217-b27c-48b9-99c4-00bd36989e1f","uuid":"190e1bd5-1677-4fe2-a02a-7a0be90e530a","timestamp":"2026-05-14T20:45:56.244Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the file docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml and extract the full text for requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4 (including their requirement groups/sections). Also look for any non_goals section. Report the complete requirement text verbatim so I can implement them.","agentId":"a5cc86d8a6b0fd2b1","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've extracted the requirements you requested. Here's the complete verbatim text for requirements R1.1 through R1.4, including their requirement group section:\n\n---\n\n## R1: Output formats and layout (default, -1, -l, -C, -x)\n\n**R1.1:**\nWhen stdout is a TTY and no format flag is given, must produce multi-column output sorted vertically (down columns, then across). Terminal width is obtained by calling pkg/sys.TerminalWidth() (int, error) — returns the current terminal column count via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl on stdout; returns an error when stdout is not a terminal. Entries are laid out by calling pkg/format.Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string — distributes entries into the maximum number of columns fitting within termWidth, with column widths computed as per-column maxima of entry lengths.\n\n**R1.2:**\nWhen stdout is not a TTY (pipe, file redirect) and no format flag is given, must produce single-column output