{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) assigned task #5202: implement `cmd/ls` with basic listing and default output corresponding to srd008-ls requirements R1.1-R1.4. This is a stitch task in a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/ls/main.go` (the ls implementation) and `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` (differential tests). The implementation must match GNU `gls` behavior for default output formats, sorting, and dot-file filtering. Git is managed externally; no git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Run Go binary and GNU reference binary (`gls`) side-by-side, compare stdout/stderr/exit code via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **TTY detection**: R1.1 requires multi-column output when stdout is TTY; R1.2 requires single-column when not TTY\n   - **pkg/sys.TerminalWidth()** returns terminal column count via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n   - **pkg/format.Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string** distributes entries into columns\n   - **C locale sorting**: All tests must set LC_ALL=C; entries sorted in C locale order\n   - **Dot-file filtering**: R1.4 - don't list entries starting with \".\" unless -a/-A given (but -a/-A flags are NOT in scope for this task)\n   - **pkg/sys.Lstat** for file metadata (handles symlinks correctly)\n   - **exec.LookPath(\"gls\")** with t.Skip if not found for graceful test skipping\n   - **40-line function limit** (E8), **500-line file limit** (E9), **no scope creep** (E3)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml** (read via Explore agent)\n     - R1.1: Multi-column output when stdout is TTY, sorted vertically (down columns, then across). Uses `pkg/sys.TerminalWidth()` and `pkg/format.Columns()`.\n     - R1.2: Single-column output (one entry per line) when stdout is not TTY (pipe/redirect).\n     - R1.3: Sort entries in C locale order (LC_COLLATE=C). Tests must set LC_ALL=C.\n     - R1.4: Don't list entries starting with \".\" unless -a or -A given (default filter).\n     - Non-goals include: --hyperlink, --dired, -Z, --quoting-style, --block-size, LS_COLORS parsing, ACL display, --group-directories-first, -w/--width, --sort=WORD\n\n   - **cmd/hostname/main.go** (read as reference pattern for cmd/ structure)\n     - Shows standard pattern: copyright header, package main, imports (fmt, os, strings, pkg/sys), const for help/version text, main() calling sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), manual arg parsing, error handling to stderr with exit code 1\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     // Implements srd047-hostname R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2.\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         // ... arg parsing, hostname lookup, output\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (inline in project_context)\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)`, `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers`\n     - `DiffTest` has fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `buildEnv()` merges test env with inherited env, sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (referenced but not inline - provides `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`)\n\n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (inline in project_context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - installs